    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for 2026-08-13 is headlined by **Miguel Vargas**, who earns our strongest daily efficiency score of 63.53. The favorable matchup against Abbott, A (xERA 5.02) provides the primary engine for this rating, further buoyed by his placement in the #3 spot and a strong 0.381 xwOBA. Joining him as a high-confidence start is **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.95), who manages to maintain elite utility despite a tougher assignment against Tolle. While **Kyle Tucker** (60.78) faces a mid-tier arm in Drohan, his consistent profile and prime position in the #4 hole make him a locked-in asset for our Roto scoring needs today.\n\nEfficiency on the margins remains a focus, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (58.88) being the most compelling value play. Despite facing the formidable Gilbert, L, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a significant 14% boost due to dynamic platoon advantages, positioning him ahead of several other options. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Wade Meckler** (42.25); while his role at the top of the order is vital for our SB scarcity strategy, he faces a high-risk scenario against the elite arm of deGrom. Our most difficult bench decision involved balancing the upside of **Andy Pages** (56.40) against the volatility of our lower-tier OF slots. **Andy Pages** narrowly missed the top tier, but remains our primary pivot should any late-scratch lineup news shift the leverage for **Luis Lara** or **Wade Meckler**. \n\nInvestors should note the structural limitations impacting our roster depth today. With **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** all scheduled for off-days and **Jordan Westburg** currently sidelined on the IL, our bench depth is severely restricted. We are proceeding without the high-floor production typically provided by those anchors, placing an even higher premium on **Sam Antonacci** to capitalize on the weak Abbott, A matchup to prevent a stagnant performance in the SB category. As always, monitors are set for official lineups to confirm the projected batting orders for **Andy Pages**, **Luis Lara**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Kyle Tucker**.",
